  "skipped": [
    {
      "name": "jellyfin",
      "language": "C#",
      "reason": "Specifications are published for every release and 10.11 -> 12.0 really breaks (routes removed, SessionInfo.NowPlayingQueueFullItems gone), but no suite of a 10.11 release exercises it: jellyfin-sdk-typescript v0.13.0's five live tests touch no changed operation, the Kotlin, C# and Python SDKs have only mocked tests, and the server's own integration tests run in-process against test-only controllers."
    },
    {
      "name": "keycloak",
      "language": "Java",
      "reason": "Every ERR-level delta between consecutive published admin API specifications (24.0.5 to 26.7.4) is a documentation fix (a status the server already returned, a renamed path parameter, a schema renamed to its existing wire name); the real breaks (identity providers leaving the realm representation, locked-out users reporting enabled, brief organization members) are behavioral and absent from the specification."
    },
    {
      "name": "directus",
      "language": "TypeScript",
      "reason": "No release pair has a structural REST break that its own suite both exercises and passes on the old release: the 11.0 policies change is behavioral and crashes the blackbox seeds before any REST call, 11.0 to 11.4 fail arm a (upstream patched the suite in 11.4.1), and the later breaks (/webhooks, /utils/hash removed, /server/health auth, inactive collections) are unexercised or behavioral."
    },
    {
      "name": "forgejo",
      "language": "Go",
      "reason": "No live-instance suite fails because of an ERR-level delta: the Forgejo specification barely changes on the wire from 7 to 16. The one exercised break found (9.0 refusing a token with no scopes, which fails forgejo-sdk v1.2.0's TestUserApp) is absent from the specification, whose CreateAccessTokenOption is identical in 8.0.3 and 9.0.3."
    }
  ]
}
